From 43a66c787ccbfda9a1d3ef53a9fe0ccd68062e16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:18:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Sun shadows with shapes: heroes, creatures, buildings and
 small things cast

The first films of the sun shadows (#263) found a broad darkening and not
one object-shaped shadow. Four faults in 0065 kept the casters a player
looks at out of the map, or out of the filter:

- Every skinned body drew far outside the map. The pass writes a caster's
  rig slot into its instance row as a float's value (37.0), and the
  caster shader read it back with bitcast<u32>, slot 1 108 606 976 for
  slot 37. Heroes, creatures, rigged game objects and animated doodads
  (trees with their own sway) all went. It now reads u32().
- Skinned gear and riders carry NoFrustumCulling, so Bevy gives them no
  Aabb, and the extract skipped every mesh without one. A skinned part is
  now bounded on its rig's origin, where its palette draws it, by its
  bind-pose box plus a margin, or a loose 3 yd sphere with no box.
- A building's interior WMO groups never cast, and they hold its walls
  and roof as often as its rooms. They cast now; props inside still don't.
- On high, the PCSS blocker search sampled a ring of six taps whose
  nearest is 0.17 yd out, and read a narrower shadow (a post's, a
  rail's) as lit. It now samples the receiver's own texel first.

The broad darkening is not the filter shading the ground itself (a test
of flat ground under the lowest sun reads 0.96 lit or better on every
slice): with the casters above missing, what darkened was the terrain's
own relief and the canopies, without the shapes standing in them.

lookshadow map <slice> | off draws a slice of the shadow map in the top
right corner, the world as the sun sees it, so the next films show what
the casters left in it.

